      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. Complex forms use r=√(x²+y²) and the argument in the appropriate quadrant, rounded as requested: q-8263 gives r=13, θ=1.176; q-86605 simplifies to 1−i, giving r=√2, θ=7π/4; q-86606 simplifies to 4/5−3i/5, giving r=1, θ=5.640; q-17521 gives r=2√5, θ=2.678; q-8076 gives r=√26, θ=6.086. The diagrams show (1,3) for q-17515 and (−4,−2) for q-8082, giving √10e^(1.249i) and 2√5e^(3.605i). Clearing denominators and matching polynomial coefficients gives q-115101: B=−2; q-73195: A=5; q-73189: A=2, B=−1; q-10995: A=−3, B=4, C=2. Expanding around the repeated root gives q-73384: (A,B,C)=(−1,−8,−6), product −48, and q-115214: (1,−2,1), product −2. For q-72339, setting t=sin(x) reduces the limit to t ln(t)→0. The cosine double-angle identity gives q-7692: cos(44°), and q-120369: cos(150°)=−√3/2. The worked solutions provide captured MA answer evidence for every field; no grade evidence was supplied.",
